  "caption": "Atmospheric circulation and net precipitation responses across AMOC recovery groups. Rows show recovery (GFDL-ESM4, NorESM2-LM, CAS-ESM2-0), non-recovery (CESM2, CNRM-ESM2-1, UKESM1-0-LL), and non-recovery minus recovery. Each group is an equal-weight mean of three fixed models. (a, c) Shading shows annual zonal-mean meridional mass streamfunction changes; contours show initial circulation, solid positive and dashed negative. Positive and negative streamfunction denote clockwise and counterclockwise circulation, respectively, in the displayed latitude-pressure sections; units are 10^9 kg s^-1. (e) Difference between group-mean streamfunction changes. (b, d) Annual net precipitation changes, P-E, where E is upward surface evaporation, including sublimation and transpiration. Green/brown indicate increased/decreased net precipitation in mm day^-1. Positive changes indicate a shift toward a more positive surface freshwater balance, not necessarily positive absolute P-E. (f) Non-recovery minus recovery net precipitation changes. Changes are experiment years 271-280 minus 1-10. In (b, d), dots indicate that all three individual-model P-E changes have the same sign; cross-hatching indicates no unanimous sign agreement, not a failed statistical test. In (e, f), dots indicate bootstrap-FDR significance and cross-hatching indicates failure: 9999 centered two-sided circular block draws, maximum p across 2/3/4-year blocks, BH q<0.05. Dots are subsampled for clarity. Circulation fields and their masks are unchanged from the precipitation version; P-E contrast significance is recomputed using P-E samples. Blue open circles and magenta crosses in (b, d) mark the initial and later latitude of maximum group-mean absolute P-E within 20S-20N, at longitudes sampled every 10 degrees. Thin grey connectors show latitude differences at the same longitude. These markers indicate net-precipitation rainband positions, not significance; they differ from the precipitation-maximum or median ITCZ indices. Initial and later periods are years1-10 and271-280, respectively.",
